-- title:
--   Iwahori U_q-cosets as unit translates of an Atkin–Lehner idele
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and work in $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$; for a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ write $\widehat\Lambda$ for its adelic box, the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}}$ generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele, $U_\Lambda=\mathrm{Stab}(\widehat\Lambda)$ for the stabiliser of $\widehat\Lambda$ in the unit group $(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}})^{\times}$, and $\Lambda^{g}=\mathbb{H}\cap g\widehat\Lambda g^{-1}$ for conjugation by a finite idele $g$ followed by intersection with $\mathbb{H}$. Let $R\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a submodule that is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ with $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ maximal orders and $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$; let $q$ and $q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$ and $q\nmid N$; assume $a<0$, $b<0$ and that $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the place $v$ dividing $q'$. Let $n$ be a finite idele in the prime Hecke set of $R$ at $q$, meaning $n\in\widehat R$, $q\,n^{-1}\in\widehat R$, $n^{-1}\notin\widehat R$ and $q^{-1}n\notin\widehat R$. Put $S=R\cap R^{n}$, and assume $S$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq$ and that $S^{n}=S$. Then: (i) for every finite idele $u$ one has $u\in U_S$ if and only if $nun^{-1}\in U_S$; (ii) for every $h$ in the set $\mathtt{uHeckeSet}\,R\,n\,q$ — that is, $h$ in the prime Hecke set of $S$ at $q$ with $(R^{n})^{h}=R$ and $R^{h}\neq R^{n}$ — there exists $u\in U_R$ with $u\notin U_S$ and $h^{-1}un\in U_S$; and (iii) conversely, every $u\in U_R\setminus U_S$ admits such an $h$ in $\mathtt{uHeckeSet}\,R\,n\,q$ with $h^{-1}un\in U_S$.
--
--   This is the coset dictionary for the Iwahori-level operator $U_q$ in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: parts (ii) and (iii) together say that the $U_q$-set of $R$ at $n$ and $U_S$ generate exactly the double coset $U_R n U_S$ with the trivial coset $nU_S$ removed, while part (i) records that the Atkin–Lehner idele $n$ normalises $U_S$. It feeds the computation of the Hecke-equivariance of the kernel map on the class set, used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.heckeKernelMap_classSetHeckeData_apply_eq_neg_comp_classSetShift`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.heckeKernelMap_classSetHeckeData_apply_eq_neg_comp_classSetShift).
